{
  "name": "synthwave-sunset",
  "vibe": "Side B, 1986. A #1a0b2e dusk sky holds a pink #ff5c8a sun disc sliced by slats that scroll upward through it, and below a #45e0ff horizon the perspective grid accelerates toward you — six horizontals eased on ph² so each widens and brightens as it arrives. Audiowide sets every headline uppercase at 0.04em; Jost carries the body. Cards are cyan-lined with a glow and stat numerals glow too. It owns Code:editor — a mac-chrome panel typing numbered lines out to a badge — and Morph:flap, a split-flap board where every character physically scaleY-flips into the next word. The camera is the hardest here: spin in the set, 8° skew, 0.65 zoom-in. Best for synths, dev tools, launch nights, retro hardware — anything that wants chrome.",
